1.501.807The "space-facing array" (18) mentioned in Stuart is an array of cover segments being capable of being opened and is enclosing the interior of a solar panel array (16), see e.g. claim 1 of Stuart, and is thus not a separate antenna array, which makes this reference irrelevant to claims of the present invention: "When the sections 20 of the space-facing array are moved apart, solar panels 16 are swung out from the interior 15 and are unfurled to their fully extended positions in a direction opposite to the direction of travel 24 of the satellite S, see page 4, lines 23-25 of Stuart.

SVG
{EMBED HERE}
2.633.037Nichols discloses an antenna including a first planar array of antenna elements and one or more side planar arrays of antenna elements, each side array adjacent to the first array and tilted at a predetermined angle relative to the first array. In an illustrative embodiment, the antenna also includes a plurality of transmit/receive modules, each module coupled to one antenna element. Each transmit/receive module includes phase shifters for varying the relative phases of the antenna elements to form a desired overall beam pattern, and a low noise amplifier and high- power amplifier for amplifying signals received and transmitted by the antenna element, respectively.
